rentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=2\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t\\right)\\right)e^{1t}+2t\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{1t}\\right)\\right),\\quad y'(t)=5\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t^2+2\\right)\\right)e^{-1t}+5(t^2+2)\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(e^{-1t}\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=2e^{1t}+ 2t(1e^{1t}),\\quad y'(t)=5(2t)e^{-1t}+5(t^2+2)(-1e^{-1t})\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=2(1+1t)e^{1t},\\quad y'(t)=5(2t-1(t^2+2))e^{-1t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{5(2t-1(t^2+2))e^{-1t}}{2(1+1t)e^{1t}}=\\frac{5(2t-1(t^2+2))}{2(1+1t)}e^{-2t}.\n$$\n\nThis derivative is defined for $t\\ne -1.$" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522917 1080 "\\frac{4}{3 e}" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522917 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522917 1083 #uuid "e69a3702-8f8e-5204-96a2-4bfcb62090f5" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522918 1080 "\\frac{5(2t-3(t^2+2))}{3(1+3t)}e^{-6t}" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522918 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522918 1083 #uuid "eb0108c7-f260-5b88-8929-4ad20ba02b21" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522919 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522913 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522919 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522919 1071 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186083240/plots/d7f3b05ffc420dbca0eff6.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=6\\left(2t{e}^{t}\\right),\\,y=4\\left({t}^{2}+2t\\right),\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522919 1072 #uuid "f38d491a-6dbf-5ea6-9e1d-28ccc7170e0f" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522919 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6\\left(2{e}^{t}(t+1)\\right),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=4\\left(2t+2\\right).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{4\\left(2t+2\\right)}{6\\left(2{e}^{t}(t+1)\\right)}=\\frac{4\\left(1\\right)}{6\\left({e}^{t}\\right)}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{4\\left(1\\right)}{6\\left({e}^{1}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\left(1\\right)}{6\\left(e\\right)}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522920 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522904 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522920 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522920 1071 "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{4t}{t+2},\\quad y=\\frac{4t^2}{t+1},\\quad t>0,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522920 1072 #uuid "fb2910a3-e9dd-5491-a8ee-7d4f932f22ed" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522920 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{4\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t\\right)\\right)(t+2)-4t\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t+2\\right)\\right)}{(t+2)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{4\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t^2\\right)\\right)(t+1)-4t^2\\left(\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(t+1\\right)\\right)}{(t+1)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{4(t+2)-4t(1)}{(t+2)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{8t(t+1)-4t^2(1)}{(t+1)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{4t+8-4t}{(t+2)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{8t^2+8t-4t^2}{(t+1)^2}\n$$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{8}{(t+2)^2},\\quad y'(t)=\\frac{4t^2+8t}{(t+1)^2}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{\\frac{4t^2+8t}{(t+1)^2}}{\\frac{8}{(t+2)^2}}=\\frac{(4t^2+8t)(t+2)^2}{8(t+1)^2}.\n$$" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522921 1080 "\\frac{(4t^2+8t)(t+2)^2}{8(t+1)^2}" 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522921 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535611 17592186045443 true] [17592186522921 1083 #uuid "febe59cd-28cc-5650-9663